<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f03700e1> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for “promoting non-traditional sexual relations” by publishing videos on social media. The videos depicted the cross-dresser in the costume of a “Winx” fairy on the territory of the Sretensky Monastery. According to the court, on the videos, “[the defendant] demonstrated transvestism by wearing clothes of the opposite sex”. The defendant explained to the court that it was his [pronouns as they appear in the court decision] everyday activity to cross-dress into the characters of “Monster High”, “Bratz”, and “Winx”, and other popular characters; he “had to hide his hobbies from his family, changed his clothes and washed off his makeup in advance, so that his family and neighbors [...] would not find out about it.”"@en .
