<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_941357af> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The managing director of the streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for the film “Triggered” (Christopher Wesley Moore, 2019). The court stated that this film contains information “promoting non-traditional sexual relations”, as it features “footage of interaction between two characters of the same biological sex (male); Viewing these scenes creates an intimate and personal mood for subsequent intersexual relations; The fragments contain depictions of romantic relationships, including images of sexual intercourse, accompanied by music and dialogue, with humorous references to the characters' non-traditional sexual preferences”. The court also mentioned that the two main characters were portrayed as “positive with a range of positive qualities, such as kindness, understanding, and responsiveness. Relationships between characters of the same biological sex are presented in a romantic vein.”"@en .
