<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_28f4a1a4> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An official at the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for distributing two films, “It's Only the End of the World” (Xavier Dolan, 2016) and “Wheel of Fortune and Fantasy” (Ryusuke Hamaguchi, 2021), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that these films contained “information and scenes demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, where two men kiss and gradually take off their clothes, as well as scenes with dialogue between characters that touch on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, in particular homosexual relations.” The company that owns the streaming service was also fined for the same films (case 05-1147/2023)."@en .
