<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f0703f0b> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“New Literary Review” was fined for publishing the book by P Faxneld “Infernal Feminism” (Series “Gender Studies”) and distributing it through the bookstore “Falanster”. The judicial expert in the case concluded that the book “contains psychological and linguistic characteristics of propaganda promoting non-traditional sexual relations and a preference for sex change, as well as psychologically influencing the reader and encouraging them to engage in LGBT relationships.” According to the case, there were 55 copies available in the store that were subsequently confiscated and destroyed."@en .
