<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_701a17bc> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company that owns the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for the films “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Dr. T & the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “Beginners” (Mike Mills, 2011), all labelled “16+”. The court found that these films “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, which is prohibited for distribution among children.” It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation."@en .
