<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8a7092d2> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The legal entity which owns the streaming service “Megafon TV” was fined for the films “Bridget Jones: The Edge of Reason” (Beeban Kidron, 2004), “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach), “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013), and “Greed” (Michael Winterbottom, 2019). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors, because they were labelled “16+”. It is not specified what scenes exactly constituted the violation."@en .
