<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_843d29d7> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The admin of the VKontakte page “Overheard at the Bar-club 'Slivki' Kazan 18+” was fined for publishing photos “promoting same-sex sexual relations (men kissing in women's clothing)”, according to the court. The judge stated that the defendant “promoted the ideology of the LGBT movement on the Internet, which is used, among other things, to destroy traditional spiritual and moral values”, and that the photos were “aimed at uniting supporters and coordinating the activities of the LGBT movement.” In court, the defendant explained that the photos were taken at “a parody theatre club where men dress up in women's clothing.” When imposing the fine, the judge took into account a mitigating circumstance – the defendant's disability."@en .
