<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_ab68dc5b> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for pictures of “men dressed in women's clothing”. According to the judicial expertise, this picture “contained psychological and linguistic signs of propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations (male homosexuality) and non-traditional sexual preferences (transvestism, transsexualism),” and that the author had “communicative goal to attract interest and form sexual attitudes, readiness for non-traditional sexual preferences and relationships.” The defendant explained that the picture depicted the band Queen during the filming of their music video “I Want to Break Free” (1984). The judge stated that “publishing this picture did not have any musical purpose given the overall meaning”. This individual was fined three times for publishing pictures on VK by the same judge on the same day."@en .
