<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8b566d88> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The online marketplace “Wildberries” was fined for several items “promoting non-traditional sexual relationships”: “2018 Calendar. Erotica-2”, the book “First Orgasm in My Life. From the ‘Diary of a Latent Lesbian’ series” by Olga Serebryanskaya, “30x40 painting on canvas on a wooden stretcher”, and “Flag/Rainbow Flag/Non-traditional Flag 90x150”. The court concluded that these items were “aimed at developing non-traditional sexual attitudes in minors” because they were sold without age restriction."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#MonitoringDec2025> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generated> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_53f9a976> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_11d88a15> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://dataout.org/ontology#Source> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6062caa7> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_7355a63a> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_84ef32a1> <https://dataout.org/ontology#uniqueCourtDocumentID> "25MS0098-01-2023-002738-26" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_dea237b5> <https://dataout.org/ontology#uniqueCourtDocumentID> "77RS0017-02-2025-014909-73" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_dcd5d3b0> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “ONIMAI: I'm Now Your Sister!” (Nekotoufu, 2017). According to the court, this manga “tells the story of a brother and sister. One morning, the brother woke up and realised he had become a girl (changed his sex). The sister, upon discovering her brother was a girl, was overjoyed and admitted it was her experiment. But instead of returning her brother to his former state, she began teaching him to be a girl. The material contains a non-episodic depiction of a female character who is a man (meaning the character was originally a male), accompanied by a positive attitude and approval. Therefore, the presented manga […] contains information promoting sex change due to the systematic distribution of graphic images containing information about sex change.” The court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
