<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_35d21bfa> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The owner of the nightclub “Edem” was fined for publishing materials on the club’s website that constituted “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations”. The ruling states that photographs published online showed “two women kissing each other, touching different parts of the body, including the chest,” which the court treated as “information aimed at forming non-traditional sexual attitudes and presenting such relations as attractive”. The same page also contained promotional descriptions of themed events, visitor statistics, and advertising language linked to adult parties. Particular attention was given to posters announcing “Night of Temptations”, a 21+ themed event, together with phrases such as “free entry for girls and couples” and programme titles including “Swinger Hot Party.” The court also cited the presence of club visitors in underwear and concluded that even the surrounding promotional language reinforced what it described as “the attractiveness of non-traditional sexuality”."@en .
