<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_23a99716> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for posting four images and a video. The four images were memes depicting “men in women's wedding dresses with the text: Why should I ask you out? I was waiting for you to make the first move. Let's split the bill. Prove and show that you need me.” The video depicted “two women on a bed kissing naked.” As the court stated, these materials “promoted non-traditional sexual relations” because the images “showed the appearance of men, which [...] culturally in Russia does not correspond to the image of a man of traditional sexual orientation”, and the video demonstrated “acceptability of sexual interaction between members of the same biological sex.” The defendant appealed the decision, but the higher instance upheld it."@en .
