<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_736c1439> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "Two women were fined for a video on social media, in which they “kissed in a cafe“, the mass media reported. According to the press office of the courts of Krasnodar Krai, the video depicted “indecent behaviour in a public place”. The court did not publish the court decision. See also case 5-54/2024."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_c2d78d1d> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The streaming platform “Okko” was held administratively liable for the film “Triggered” (2019, Christopher Moore). The judicial expertise established that “the genre, plot, and expressive means used [in the film] aimed at fostering a positive attitude toward non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences; The depicted same-sex relationships and the storyline are structured in such a way as to create a socio-psychological attitude not only toward the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences, but also to foster a distorted perception of the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relationships”. The deputy general director of the streaming platform was also fined for the same film (see case 5-1663/2025-162)."@en .
