<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_c282acec> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a meme in 2019: “a picture depicting a cat holding a flag in its mouth; The flag consists of six stripes, the colors of which run from top to bottom: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple; At the bottom of the photograph is the text 'naturalu po ***(expletive)' ['smack a straight guy in the face'].” The court mentioned tha tthe flag was a “symbol of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'”. The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), which is expressed through a call to action to defend non-traditional relationships against the 'straights' as worthy of being recognized and valued more highly than 'straight' relationships; [...] sexual relationships not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for the forceful assertion of one's right to them against heterosexuals.” The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown."@en .
