<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_47427112> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A moderator of a VKontakte page was fined, becasue the page “contained text, images, audio, and video […] prohibited for distribution among children, namely, information aimed at denying traditional spiritual, moral, and family values and promoting non-traditional sexual relations”, according to the court. The judicial expertise concluded: “the main theme of this webpage is the recognition of the normality and equivalence of sexual relations between a man and a man, in connection with which indirect signs of distorted ideas about the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relations are present.” In court, the defendant explained that this VK page was about dating among homosexual people. The exact content that constituted the violation is unknown."@en .
