<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#mentioned_in_4a4b9a47> <https://schema.org/archivedAt> <https://web.archive.org/web/20260416175603/https://mosregtoday.ru/news/power/na-videoservis-wink-sostavili-protokol-za-rasprostranenie-informatsii-o-netraditsionnyh-tsennostjah/?ysclid=mo1r2rvjr0650208962> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_28e9ca77> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “Fujoshi Haru-chan wa Osake Suki” (Yasai, 2018). From the court decision: “This material contains information about a yaoi manga (a genre that depicts romantic and/or sexual relationships between men) [...] it is presented with a description indicating the non-traditional nature of the main characters' sexual relationships [...] the combination of the manga description and its cover contains information promoting non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences.” Furthermore, the court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
