<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_0479dc42> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “The Color of Sin: An Innocent Sin 2” (Oh Gye, 2024). According to the court, this manga “tells the story of a young man named Noah, who finds a place where no one knows him to live a normal life with his girlfriend, Nayeon, and two male friends in an open relationship. This material contains non-episodic depictions of non-traditional sexual relationships between characters, represented by several illustrations of supporting male characters (Noah's friends) in romantic and sexual contexts: touching, hugging, sexual interaction, etc.” The court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
