<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f8b290c1> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The film distribution company “Russian Report” was fined for airing the TV series “Episodes” (David Crane and Jeffrey Klarik, 2011) on the “KinoLiving” TV channel with the label “16+”. The court stated that the series contained “the demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations expressed by a visual component: the depiction of sensual interaction between two persons of the same biological sex (female), namely: a prolonged kiss expressing sexual passion; caressing movements of the hand of one woman on the chest area of the other.” It is said that this judicial expertise was based on the “classification of kisses”, which was also mentioned in the case 5-1073/23. Earlier, the editor-in-chief of the TV channel was also fined for distributing the TV series (case 5-1000/23)."@en .
