<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_95ce77bb> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for Instagram posts, which the court found to be “deviant in nature, since the publications are published for an unlimited number of people and differ from generally accepted and established norms of behavior in ordinary society, promoting non-traditional sexual relations, including among minors.” Among the pieces of evidence are “comments on the new bill banning LGBT propaganda in the Russian Federation”, the image of “a tattoo of a dog with a rainbow flag (pride flag) with the inscription ‘gay dog’”, and “a publication with an image of the country's top officials with the inscription on the rainbow flag (pride flag) in English ‘GAY FRIENDLY BAR. MAKE SEX NOT WAR’.”  The court also mentioned that there were publications “discrediting the Russian army” (a separate administrative offence, Article 20.3.3). As the defendant shared with the media, two police officers came to her home following a complaint filed against her and asked her to show the tattoo on her shoulder, which depicted a dog wearing a rainbow scarf."@en .
