<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_3f2d2764> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The editor-in-chief of the “KinoLiving” TV channel was fined after Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that the TV channel aired the series “Made in Italy” (Camilla Nesbitt, 2019). According to Roskomnadzor, “the series contained images that touch on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations (kisses between two people of the same biological sex (male), as well as dialogue between the characters that touches on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations.” The company that owns the TV channel was also fined for the same content (case 05-1133/2023)."@en .
