<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_d4df5fc7> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual who attended a drag performance at a Halloween party in the nightclub “Dark Horse” in Yaroslavl  was fined after the police raided the club. The details of this case are unknown; the court did not publish the decision. The defendant appealed, but the decision was upheld by the Leninsky District Court of Yaroslavl (case 12-70/2025). The mass media reported that during the raid, the police forced the club's visitors to lie on the floor for several hours; some people were beaten; several performers were detained, and seven administrative cases were initiated. We found eight such cases on the court website, six of which resulted in a punishment. This is one of these cases."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_3029f15a> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtDocumentDate> "2025-04-29"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_48856780> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtDocumentDate> "2023-10-18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_02380185> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for the film “Yves Saint Laurent” (Jalil Lespert, 2014). According to the Head of the St. Petersburg courts press office, there were multiple scenes identified in the film containing “propaganda of LGBT”, including these scenes: “two people of the same sex passionately kissing; '–What a cutie he is! –Forget it! He's into guys; -Where are the bedrooms?, -There's only one, -So you're together?, -Yes”; “two people of the same biological sex kissing, accompanied by a voice-over commentary 'I believed in the cult of fidelity, but with you everything happened incredibly quickly'.” The deputy general director of this streaming service was also fined for the same film (case 5-837/2024-162)."@en .
