<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_bafdf4fa> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for four videos published on her personal page in 2011. The court found these videos “extremist” and “containing signs of propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations or preferences related to the LGBT community”, because they depicted “kisses between a man and a man”. Another individual was fined by the same court for similar content (case 5-207/2025)."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_51351717> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The project manager at “Mangalib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was prosecuted for several publications. The publication in this case is “The Time My Friend Wanted to Try a Skirt” (Terai Akane, 2019). The court stated that it “contained non-episodic depictions of a male character wearing traditionally feminine clothing and accessories, which is accompanied by positive attitudes and approval; description and depiction of non-traditional sexual relationships between the characters, represented by several illustrations of the two main male characters in a romantic context: touching, holding hands, etc.” This individual was fined at least 12 times for different publications. The company “MangaLib” was also fined at least 12 times."@en .
