<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6ac106d9> <https://dataout.org/ontology#concernsLegalArticle> <https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_2_part_2> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_5494bd00> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company “DotDTechnology”, which owns the TV channel “Clubbing TV”, was issued a warning for airing six music videos: “Muchas” by Myd feat. Cola Boyy (2018), “Smile” by Galantis (2013), “Ride It” by Regard (2019), “La Lueur” by Holism (2022), “Hold Me To The Light” by KAS:ST (2021), and “You Boy” by Arigato Massaï feat. Yanis (2020). According to the court, these videos “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relationships and preferences to minors” because they were labelled “16+”. The judge decided to replace a fine with a warning because it was the company's first-time administrative offence. However, later, the company was fined by the same court for airing other music videos (see case 05-0475/2023)."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_c5caec32> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtDocumentDate> "2023-11-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
