<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8b1ac68a> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The deputy general director of the online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for distributing the film “Triggered” (2019, Christopher Moore). The judicial expertise established that “the genre, plot, and expressive means used [in the film] aimed at fostering a positive attitude toward non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences; The depicted same-sex relationships and the storyline are structured in such a way as to create a socio-psychological attitude not only toward the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences, but also to foster a distorted perception of the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relationships”. The streaming platform was also fined for the same film (see case 5-1661/2025)."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_courts#25KJ0009> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtCode> "25KJ0009" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#55347> <https://schema.org/url> <https://www.themoviedb.org/movie/55347> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6e719509> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for a 7-second TikTok video. According to the court, the video showed “a young man with long hair, headphones, glasses and a black T-shirt, accompanied by text placed on screen”. The exact text is unknown. Police testified that the clip had already been deleted from TikTok by the time of the inspection, but had continued circulating on Telegram channels, where it was then examined and used as evidence. The same individual was prosecuted at least 7 times for different TikTok videos."@en .
