<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_a0fded80> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for dressing in women’s clothing in a public place. The court interpreted that as “promoting non-traditional sexual relations by appearance and behaviour. [...] while in a public place, positioned himself as a female, was dressed in women's clothing, had makeup on his face, and had manicure on his fingernails. He thereby promoted non-traditional sexual relations and committed actions aimed at fostering non-traditional sexual attitudes, the attractiveness of non-traditional sexual relations, and a distorted idea of ​​the social equivalence of traditional and non-traditional sexual relations.” This individual was fined twice for wearing “women's clothing” (see aslo 5-415/2025)."@en .
