<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8d51dd6d> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://dataout.org/ontology#MonitoringRecord> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8d51dd6d> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “Sex Life With My Beast Partner” (Komagome, 2018). According to the court, this manga “tells the story of a girl who tries to stay away from therianthropes (beast-like creatures) at the company where she works. She has been dating her boyfriend, Mitsuru, for a year. But one day, she discovers his secret: he is a therianthrope. Despite their differences, the girl does not reject him, but rather, enters into an intimate relationship with him. The material contains non-episodic depictions of non-traditional sexual relationships, represented by several illustrations of a female person (the main character) with a beast-like creature (perceived as an animal) in a romantic and erotic context: kisses, hugs, sensual touches, and sexually explicit actions.” The court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
