<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f2235dda> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The deputy general director for content on the streaming service “Ivi” was fined for the films “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Dr. T & the Women” (Robert Altman, 2000), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “Beginners” (Mike Mills, 2011) with the age restriction label “16+”. The court mentioned that these films contained “scenes describing homosexual relationships between men and [...] women, as well as references to homosexual relationships” demonstrating “non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” among minors. It is not specified which scenes exactly constituted the violation. The company that owns the streaming service was also fined for the same films (case 05-0902/2023)."@en .
