<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_82742d5b> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasTriggerObject> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#social_media_061> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_883fb9e0> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasTriggerObject> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#17203> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_08defc73> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://dataout.org/ontology#Source> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#OL40980640W> <https://schema.org/name> "“Straight Talk About Homosexuality. The Other Side of Tolerance” (Richard Cohen) "@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_c7287c9b> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was prosecuted for “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, sex change” by wearing “women's clothing and a wig” in public. The residents of the village of Varfolomeevka (population around 1K) called the police after noticing this person on the street, as reported by the press office of the Ministry of Internal Affairs for Primorsky Krai. Other details of the case are unknown; the court did not publish the decision text."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#MonitoringDec2025> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#generated> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_aafc0f08> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#official_0001> <https://dataout.org/ontology#defendantCategory> <https://dataout.org/ontology#official> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f7f20549> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasDefendant> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#official_0029> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8de1ce86> <https://dataout.org/ontology#mentionedIn> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#mentioned_in_e9f92480> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_205ff6a3> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for distributing ten films: “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016), “Bridget Jones: The Edge of Reason” (Beeban Kidron, 2004), “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013), “Easy A” (Will Gluck, 2010), “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001), “Compartment No. 6” (Juho Kuosmanen, 2021), “Greed” (Michael Winterbottom, 2019), “Green Book” (Peter Farrelly, 2018), “The Amusement Park” (the title translated from Russian, the exact film is unknown), and “Beanpole” (Kantemir Balagov, 2019). According to the court, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences to minors” and should have been marked “18+” instead of “16+”. The court did not specify the exact scenes in these movies that constituted the violation."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#mentioned_in_9b589cd3> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "News.ru"@ru .
