<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_0dfd46d0> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The deputy general director of the company “M3” was fined for distributing two films on the company's streaming service “More.tv”, labelled “16+”: “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013) and “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001). In both films, experts from Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found  scenes “demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations” among minors. In the first film, these scenes include the appearance of a transgender character and dialogs about transition (the exact time codes are 00:56:57-00:58:20, 00:58:21-00:58:52, 01:00:12-01:01:33, 01:01:34-01:02:10, 01:02:11-01:03:29, 01:04:14-01:04:22, 01:06:19-01:06:34, 01:10:32-01:11:00). In the second, there was one scene (01:21:47-01:21:57), in which “two characters of the same sex (female) kissing in a sexual context.”"@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#social_media_482b9013> <https://dataout.org/ontology#triggerObjectCategory> <https://dataout.org/ontology#socialMediaPost> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_8c72027a> <https://schema.org/addressRegion> <https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_regions#77> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_392b97e6> <https://dataout.org/ontology#monitoredIncidentYear> "2025"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f0bf5009> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing six videos between 2012 and 2015: the music video “Cliffs Edge” by Hayley Kiyoko (2015) and other videos titled “boys kissing”, “Takumi-kun 2. Rainbow glow”, “U”, “Miles & Kyler”, “boys are being naughty”. The court pointed out that each of these videos depicted kisses either between two men or two women; these videos were “related to the promotion of non-traditional sexual relations of the LGBT community” and were of “an extremist nature”."@en .
