<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_0549f459> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company “Elton John”, which owns the queer bar “Elton bar” in Novosibirsk, was fined for five posts on Telegram and one video on YouTube. The judicial expert who analysed the content concluded that the video “contains signs of propaganda of the LGBT movement”, because in the video, it was said that “participating in a gay community and visiting gay clubs is a way to achieve social success and psychological comfort.” The defence argued that the company neither produced nor published the video; it was made by a YouTube blogger. However, the court dismissed this argument, stating that the company's director participated in the video. In the Telegram posts, the expert found “images of a six-stripe rainbow”, which constituted “signs of LGBT propaganda”. The defence denied that the Telegram posts were published by the company, but the judge stated that “there was no doubt” that the posts were made “on behalf of and in the interests” of the company."@en .
