<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_74de56cd> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The deputy general director of the online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for distributing the film “Black Ghosts” (Andreas Marawell, 2015), labelled “16+”. The court mentioned the timecodes of four scenes, which “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and preferences” to minors: 00:11:10-00:12:57; 00:15:46-00:16:54; 01:33:41-01:35:07; 01:29:19-01:31:42. It is not specified what these scenes depicted."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_a6c30668> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The project manager at “Mangalib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was prosecuted for several publications. The publication in this case is “ONIMAI: I'm Now Your Sister!” (Nekotoufu, 2017). According to the court, this publication “contains images purportedly dealing with the theme of transgender transition, contains information about manga with the subgenre of gender intrigue, where a man, for one reason or another, pretends to be a girl or vice versa” and “contains a non-episodic depiction of a female character who is a man, that is, was originally a male character, which is accompanied by positive attitude and approval.” This individual was fined at least 12 times for different publications. The company “MangaLib” was also fined at least 12 times."@en .
