<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_cd366232> <https://dataout.org/ontology#penaltyValue> _:nb339817b2c8941f983f86810fb398ca2b216 .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_da52ce2a> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “Revolutionary Girl Utena: The Adolescence of Utena” (Be-Papas, 1999). According to the court's description, “the comic's main character [...] experienced a breakup with her lover, after which she decided to appear before people as a man. [...] The princess falls in love with [the main character] and doesn't hide her feelings: the girls kiss and spend time together.” The court stated that this comic “can be classified as a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations)”. This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
