<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_4d9dc24e> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company “DotDTechnology”, which owns the TV channel “Clubbing TV”, was fined for airing three music videos: “Flash” by Lewis OfMan (2018), “For Love” by filous feat. klei (2018), and “La Lueur” by Holism (2022). According to the court, these videos “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relationships and preferences to minors” because they were labelled “16+”. It is not specified what scenes exactly constituted the violation."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_2c8f19ca> <https://dataout.org/ontology#mentionedIn> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#mentioned_in_06b5b7c3> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#social_media_029> <https://schema.org/identifier> "social_media_029" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_883fb9e0> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The online streaming service “Tricolor Kino i TV Online” was fined for showing the film “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach) labelled “16+” with a 10-second scene (01:21:47-01:21:57) of “two same-sex characters (female) kissing in a sexual context”, which the court found to be the “demonstration of non-traditional sexual relationships to minors.”"@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f10b9779> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The general director of a bar was fined because the bar's page on VKontakte advertised a “venue intended for people of non-traditional sexual orientation”. The judicial expert mentioned that the bar's VK page “promoted the ideology of the LGBT movement prohibited in the Russian Federation.” The exact content that constituted the violation is unknown."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6711ac2b> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasPenalty> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#pen_fine_f319bbe5> .
