<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_4e165520> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for the film “Triggered” (Christopher Wesley Moore, 2019). As experts from Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, concluded, the film “demonstrated information with the signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation and [...] ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations and (or) preferences).” The managing director of the streaming service was also fined for the same film (see case 5-647/2025)."@en .
