<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_ebed1283> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The editor-in-chief of the streaming service “Tricolor Kino i TV Online” was fined for the film “The Key Game” (Vicente Villanueva, 2022). Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, identified ten scenes constituting the violation: “two girls, feigning passion, hint at the permissibility of sexual interaction between members of the same biological sex” (00:22:59-00:25:45); “a dialogue indicating the non-traditional sexual preferences of one of the characters” (00:44:35-00:45:40); “a dialogue touching on non-traditional sexual preferences and the feelings of one man for another” (00:56:25-00:58:16); “a scene showing the male characters walking in a park [...] confessing their feelings to each other” (01:01:37-01:02:25); “a scene that reveals a connection and love between two men” (01:04:08-01:04:49); “kissing male characters (01:28:20-01:28:46); “sexual interaction between two men” (01:28:49-01:29:09); “a scene of sexual intercourse between two men” (01:31:05-01:31:18); “scenes of simulated sexual intercourse” (01:28:11-01:29:38, 01:31:17-01:33:36); “a scene of a marriage between representatives of the same biological sex, two women and two men” (01:38:10-01:41:47)."@en .
