<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_9bf237ed> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “With You, Our Love Will Make It Through” (Yuzuki Chihiro, 2021). According to the court, this manga “tells a story of a young girl, Mari, who lives in a city where beast-like creatures and humans coexist. One day, the girl meets Tsunagu, a beast-like creature, and this initial encounter confuses her. But as she gets to know him better, she becomes deeply attracted to him, despite their differences. The material contains a non-episodic depiction of a non-traditional sexual relationship between the main character, represented by several illustrations of a female figure with a beast-like creature (perceived as an animal) in a romantic context: kisses, hugs, and sensual touching.” The court stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
