<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_28a5d9ba> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The TV channel “START World” was fined for “demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences” by showing the film “Babysitting” (Philippe Lacheau, 2014), labelled “16+”. The judicial expertise identified two scenes in the film, which “depicted kisses between people of the same biological sex (female)”. According to the experts, “there was a sensual (non-conventional) kiss in the film, which is a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations.”"@en .
