<https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_courts#27RS0006> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtCode> "27RS0006" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_cc6462d8> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The TV channel “KINO TV” was fined for “distributing among minors” the film “V for Vendetta” (James McTeigue, 2006), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, which carried out judicial expertise, found four scenes in the film “demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations.” Such scenes “expressed verbal (description) and visual components (images of kisses, hugs between persons of the same biological sex (female).” Earlier, the editor-in-chief of this TV channel was fined for the same film (see case 12-1609/2023)."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_0d918d42> <https://dataout.org/ontology#courtDocumentDate> "2025-07-31"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
