<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_c2270492> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The director general of the company “Restrim Media” that owns the streaming service “Wink” was fined for making the films “Bridget Jones: The Edge of Reason” (Beeban Kidron, 2004), “Curse of Chucky” (Don Mancini, 2013), and “Blow Dry” (2001, Paddy Breathnach) publicly acessible to minors, because they were labelled “16+”. According to Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, such as passionate kissing between two women, a scene where women are about to engage in virtual sex via video call.” Earlier, the company was also fined for the same films (see case 05-0486/2023)."@en .
