<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_84701b32> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for several Instagram posts that depicted two women kissing, embracing, and touching each other. The accompanying captions were: “This is an ad for my handbag with foxes”, “1 year V O, what a year it has been! Others don’t experience this much in five years. Thank you for making me happy,” as well as photographs labelled “Wife and wife.” Other posts showed the pair holding hands next to a white poster with wedding-ring illustrations and captions like “We have been together for 2 years. I love you,” “Three years! She came up with the name for this anniversary — Flirtovshchina© Thank you for being ebanuty [fucked up] together©,” and a photo of a couple embracing with the caption: “My little pumpkin, my sweet eclair, the syrup to my potatoes! Now you are also a woman 35+. Happy birthday.”"@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_f5b264b5> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The editor-in-chief of the “KinoLiving” TV channel was fined after Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that the TV channel aired the series “Episodes” (David Crane and Jeffrey Klarik, 2011), which “contained information demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences expressed by a visual component: an image of sensual interaction between two persons of the same biological sex (female), prolonged kisses and caresses of two women.”"@en .
