<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_4400eabf> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a picture of “two kissing women and symbols similar to those of the extremist organisation 'LGBT movement'” in 2019. The court described the picture as “two women standing next to each other, kissing in the courtyard of a residential building, covered with a cloth consisting of stripes placed on top in the order: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, purple.” The judicial expert concluded that the picture depicts positevely “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman), [...] it is expressed visually (the viewer is shown that this is beautiful, aesthetically pleasing, and therefore good and acceptable); [...] sexual relations not between a man and a woman are presented as acceptable for public display, on par with heterosexual ones.” The exact picture is unknown. The same individual was fined five times on the same day by the same court for publishing pictures on VK. The media reported that the first-instance court imposed a 100,000 RUB fine for each case. The higher-instance court reduced the fine, but the amount is unknown."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#individual_0070> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Person> .
