<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_40142de8> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_39122cc9> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#source_944a989a> <https://dataout.org/ontology#uniqueCourtDocumentID> "77RS0026-02-2024-003735-25" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_ab6be87c> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The TV channel “TV-21M” was fined for broadcasting four films, labelled “16+”: “García y García” (2021, Ana Murugarren), “Saint Amour” (2016, Benoît Delépine and Gustave Kervern), “The In-Laws” (2003, Andrew Fleming), and “8 Dates” (2008, Peris Romano and Rodrigo Sorogoyen). In the court’s view, these films “demonstrated non-traditional sexual relations” among minors. In “García y García”, the court found such “demonstration” in the scene, which shows two female characters kissing on the neck and lips and contains the line “Darling, you’re the one who doesn’t want to come out”. In “Saint Amour”, the court identified the scene, in which two female characters “merge in a sensual kiss”. In “The In-Laws”, the court mentioned the scene, in which “the initiator of the kiss had a romantic interest in another man, but tried to deny his non-traditional sexual orientation”. In “8 Dates”, the “demonstration” scene was “two heterosexual couples, as well as a young man named Alfonso, kiss according to the rules of the game”. When analysing the first two films, the court applied the so-called “classification of kisses”, which categorises kisses “depending on the kinds of feelings”, for example “kisses of affection, tenderness, respect, and love”."@en .
