<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_bb5601c1> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A VKontakte user was fined for publishing a meme, which the court described as “the presidents of the United States and Russia lying in the same bed, with the following dialogue: '[Name redacted] - Will you recognise [Address redacted, most likely Crimea] for sure? [Name redacted] - Of course, dear!'” According to the court, this photo “was aimed at promoting LGBT and non-traditional sexual orientation.” The exact image is unknown. The amount of the fine has been redacted from the court ruling. This individual was fined four times by the same judge on the same day for posting on VK."@en .
