<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_bbd0f805> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A Moscow resident was fined after police monitoring identified two archived photographs on the defendant’s social media page, originally uploaded in 2017, depicting two naked women kissing and embracing. The court treated the images as unlawful because they remained publicly accessible in 2025 and concluded that their continued presence online constituted the dissemination of prohibited information. In addition to the photographs themselves, the ruling states that the page also displayed what authorities described as extremist symbolism — specifically “a flag consisting of six stripes”, characterised as the symbol of an organisation associated with “non-traditional sexual relations”, the dissemination of which is prohibited under anti-extremism legislation following the 2023 Supreme Court decision on the “international LGBT movement.”"@en .
