<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_4843a6c5> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An official at the streaming service “Kinopoisk” was fined for distributing two films, “Breaking Up in Rome” (Edoardo Leo, 2021) and “Clouds of Sils Maria” (Olivier Assayas, 2014), labelled “16+”. Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator, found that these films contained “information and scenes demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, where men kiss on the lips, as well as scenes with dialogue between characters that touch on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences, in particular homosexual relations.”"@en .
