<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_0e2832f3> <https://dataout.org/ontology#concernsLegalArticle> <https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_part_7> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6d20f1f4> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for a TikTok video. According to the court, the video showed “a young man with long hair, headphones, glasses and a black T-shirt, accompanied by text placed on screen”. The exact text is unknown. The court held that the caption, together with the music, was sufficient to disseminate “propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations”. The same individual was prosecuted at least 7 times for different TikTok videos."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_e3ed6727> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for posting “a voice message, accompanied by a video recording, which depicts two women kissing” on Telegram. The judicial expert concluded that the content “presented same-sex female love in an attractive way (this is the type of relationship preferred by bloggers, fashionable and stylish-looking attractive modern women who live in stylish interiors);” and that it presented “non-traditional sexual relations (not between a man and a woman) [...] in an attractive manner.” The exact content that constituted the violation is unknown. The post is dated 06.02.2025. The same individual was fined at least six times on the same day by the same judge for posting similar content on Telegram and Instagram."@en .
