<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_95025123> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The bookshop “Falanster” was fined for selling six books: “More Happy Than Not” (Adam Silvera, 2015), “The Fruit of Knowledge” (Liv Strömquist, 2014), “The Miseducation of Cameron Post” (Emily Danforth, 2012), “Infernal Feminism” (Per Faxneld, 2022), “Fence, Vol. 2” (C. S. Pacat, 2019), and “Everybody: A Book About Freedom” (Olivia Lang, 2021). The judicial expertise established that these books “contain psychological and linguistic signs of propaganda for non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences and/or gender reassignment, and also contain incitement to involvement in LGBT relationships.” The general director of the bookshop was also fined by the same judge on the same day for distributing the same books (see case 05-0269/2025)."@en .
