<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_c2d72669> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for the film “Abduction 101” (Steve Noir, Robin Entreinger, 2019), because it “contained a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relations and (or) preferences”, as the mass media reported. It is unknown what scenes exactly constituted the violation; the court did not publish the decision text. Earlier, the deputy general director of this streaming platform was also fined for the same film (see case 5-683/2025-162)."@en .
