<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_7046d4eb> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company “M3”, which owns the streaming service “More.tv”, was fined for distributing the series “The Shannara Chronicles” (Alfred Gough, Miles Millar, 2016), labelled “16+”. The judicial experts identified six scenes, which “indirectly demonstrate non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences.” The experts added that “along with the dialogues and general development of relationships between the women throughout the series, their interactions are perceived by the recipient as a demonstration of non-traditional sexual relationships and/or preferences.” The mentioned scenes were: 28:20-29:43 (E1S2), 23:46-25:25 (E2S2), 32:10-32:37 (E2S2), 16:34-16:42 (E4S2), 19:27-21:18 (E9S2), 34:53-35:15 (E10S2). Earlier, the product manager of this streaming service was fined for the same TV series (see case 5-1189/23)."@en .
