<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_d1ed7fcb> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for posting a meme on VKontakte, which depicted a drawing of Quentin Tarantino with a quote attributed to him, “Making movies and not children is my motto”. In court, the defendant explained that she had uploaded the image in 2021 because she liked Tarantino and, at that time, associated the quotation with prioritising work over family rather than rejecting parenthood. She also stated that she had lost access to the account in 2022 and could not delete the post. This ruling has been reported as the first known fine imposed under Russia’s ban on the so-called “childfree propaganda,” introduced by the November 2024 amendments to Article 6.21."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_066700be> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An individual was fined for posts on Telegram. The exact content that constituted the violation is not mentioned. The judge stated that “the dissemination of beliefs and preferences regarding sexual orientation and specific forms of sexual relations should not infringe on the dignity of others or call into question public morality as understood in Russian society.”"@en .
