<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_e5c9cf4d> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "“MangaLib”, a platform for online comics and manga, was fined for publications on its website. The publication in this case is “The Time My Friend Wanted to Try a Skirt” (Terai Akane, 2019). From the court decision: “This material, presented in Volume 1, tells the story of two childhood friends (both male), one of whom decides to feminise his image by repeatedly (in different chapters) wearing women's clothing and accessories. He is partly assisted in this by a close friend, who witnesses the transformations. For example, in Chapter 10 of Volume 1, the character decides to wear a wedding dress, and the two have a photo shoot in a church. Meanwhile, one friend admires the other, thinking about how happy he would be if he had such a beautiful bride. The material contains a non-episodic depiction of a male character in traditionally feminine clothing and accessories, accompanied by a positive attitude and approval. Furthermore, the material contains descriptions and depictions of non-traditional sexual relationships between the characters, represented by several illustrations of the two main male characters in a romantic context: touching, holding hands, etc.” The court also stated that “the information displayed can be classified as revealing signs of a socio-cultural threat to the national security of the Russian Federation in terms of the protection of traditional values, since it reveals signs of ideological and psychological influence on the recipient in the form of the imposition of a destructive ideology (propaganda of non-traditional sexual relations).” This is one of at least 12 cases in a serial persecution of “MangaLib”. The manager of “MangaLib” was also prosecuted at least 12 times for different publications."@en .
