<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_d8a9e2d0> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The company “Channel One. Worldwide”, a subdivision of the state-controlled federal TV channel that owns another TV channel, “Dom Kino”, was fined for airing the film “B-Day!” (Roman Karimov, 2018), labelled “16+”. According to the court, the film “contained conflict-provoking scenes touching on the topic of non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences and should have been labelled 18+.” The exact scenes that constituted the violation are not specified."@en .
