<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_e1ab2ef5> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A drag performer was fined after the police raided the nightclub “Dark Horse” in Yaroslavl. The court stated that the defendant “wore women's clothing and feminine makeup, demonstrating his appearance to an indefinite number of people, thereby committing public actions aimed at developing non-traditional sexual attitudes”. In court, the performer explained that he was detained while on stage and that his costume symbolised the Coronavirus because it was a Halloween party. The defendant appealed the first-instance decision twice (Magistrate Court No. 3 of the Leninsky Judicial District of Yaroslavl). However, both instances upheld it. The mass media reported that during the raid, the police forced the club's visitors to lie on the floor for several hours; some people were beaten; several performers were detained, and seven administrative cases were initiated. We found eight such cases on the court website, six of which resulted in a punishment. This is one of these cases."@en .
