<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_14d43d58> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The online streaming platform “Okko” was fined for 16 films. According to the Head of the St. Petersburg courts press office, the court found “bad things” in the following films: “The Miseducation of Cameron Post” (Desiree Akhavan, 2018), “Bridget Jones: The Edge of Reason” (Beeban Kidron, 2004), “Perfect Strangers” (Paolo Genovese, 2016), “Three Many Weddings” (Javier Ruiz Caldera, 2013), “Black Swan” (Darren Aronofsky, 2010), “The New Mutants” (Josh Boone, 2020), “Blow Dry” (Paddy Breathnach, 2001), “Easy A” (Will Gluck, 2010), “Zwanger & Co” (Johan Nijenhuis, 2022), “Clouds of Sils Maria” (Olivier Assayas, 2014), “Breaking Up in Rome” (Edoardo Leo, 2021), “The Imitation Game” (Morten Tyldum, 2014), “Little Italy” (Donald Petrie, 2018), “Alexander” (Oliver Stone, 2004), “Love Is Love Is Love” (Eleanor Coppola, 2021), and “The Royal Tenenbaums” (Wes Anderson, 2001). It is unknown what scenes exactly in these films constituted the violation."@en .
