<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_bcdd50f4> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "An Uzbekistan citizen was fined and ordered to leave the country for posting “text messages about the provision of intimate services for non-traditional relationships” on VKontakte. The court stated that the messages “promoted non-traditional sexual relations and preferences” because their author “has a homosexual position ('vers', 'pass'), sexual orientation - gay,” and they were accompanied by “a nude photo of a man offering non-traditional sexual relations.”"@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#1137746363150> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/Organization> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_1fb16368> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The legal entity “Inetra”, which owned the streaming service “Peers.TV”, was fined for “demonstration of materials containing LGBT scenes to minors”, according to mass media. The exact content that constituted the violation is unknown. An administrative protocol against the company was drawn up by Roskomnadzor, the Russian mass media regulator."@en .
