<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_599a93d6> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The streaming platform “IVI” was fined for distributing the South Korean TV series “The One and Only” (2021). The court held that the series contained scenes “demonstrating non-traditional sexual relations through the backstory of two female characters whose past romantic attachment is gradually revealed through memory scenes, dialogue, and visual detail”. According to the ruling, prohibited content included scenes in which one woman “gently strokes the hand” of another, memories of how the two women once planned “to leave together for one of the European countries so that they could avoid hiding their relationship from others,” and a later confrontation in which one character openly states: “We loved each other.” The court further stressed that “the totality of all the above-listed scenes … helps the recipient create a picture of non-traditional sexual relations,” and concluded that, given “the systemic thinking of the recipient,” these fragments constituted prohibited demonstration of same-sex relations."@en .
