<https://dataout.org/rdf/reference/ru_law#article_6_21_2_part_3> <https://schema.org/description> "Distributing information among minors demonstrating “non-traditional sexual relations and/or preferences”, including descriptions or depictions of such preferences, or information “capable of causing minors to desire to change their sex” by a foreign national or stateless person. Does not apply to cases covered by part 6 of Article 6.21. Punishment: RUB 50K–100K fine with administrative expulsion from Russia, or detention for up to 15 days with subsequent expulsion."@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_50ca2710> <https://dataout.org/ontology#monitoredIncidentYear> "2024"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#unclear_005> <https://schema.org/identifier> "unclear_005" .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#mentioned_in_7fc5ea83> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Kommersant.ru"@en .
<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_6b264a42> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "The journalist Elena Klimova created the online support project “Children-404. LGBT-teenagers”, which included groups on social media, in which queer teens shared their experiences and sought support. The project regularly published their letters. The court determined that the project’s content constituted unlawful promotion of same-sex relationships among minors. In 2025, the European Court of Human Rights ruled that the decision of the Russian court violates the Articles 8 and 10 of the ECHR."@en .
