<https://dataout.org/rdf/data/project-6-21#record_b94ab3d4> <https://dataout.org/ontology#hasSnippet> "A Moscow resident was fined for a VKontakte video titled “Gay skinhead 88.” The ruling states that the video was publicly available and treated as unlawful solely because of its title and its association with “LGBT propaganda.” The judgment does not describe the video’s content in detail, nor explain whether the material was explicit, documentary, ironic, musical, or archival in character — only that police classified it as “promoting non-traditional relations” after discovering it during online monitoring. The same individual was fined at least twice for different online content. "@en .
